{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Be a</b> — like a refuge to hide in; therefore after it [comes] \"to come always,\" for every refuge is on high." "<b>And the meaning of \"I have commanded\"</b> — either Samuel promised him, or in the sense of \"He commanded and it stood,\" like the word of HaShem, the meaning referring to decrees through the angels."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 71, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:49.041373087Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}